From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server, shell32, advpack: an administrator's split token (Limited, Administrators for deny only, linked Full token)

On Windows an administrator's ordinary token is the filtered half of a split token:
- elevation type Limited, not elevated;
- Administrators present only for deny (SE_GROUP_USE_FOR_DENY_ONLY);
- an ordinary user's privileges and integrity;
- a linked full token (elevation type Full), which consent hands out.
A member of sg-admins (the server's SG_ADMIN_GROUP can name another group) had a standard user's
token: Default, no Administrators, no linked token. Installers that look for a split token to
decide whether to ask for elevation (Mozilla's NSIS UAC plugin) never asked.
Now an unelevated administrator's token is Limited with a deny-only Administrators group, and an
elevated person's token is Full. Their TokenLinkedToken is the other half. A standard user's
stays Default with no linked token.
The linked token is the person's own at identification level. Unless SYSTEM asks for it, the
handle only queries it: it can't be used to impersonate or to make a process token. Rights still
come only through consent (the elevation broker).
A deny-only group still matches deny ACEs. IsUserAnAdmin and advpack's IsNTAdmin count only an
enabled Administrators group.
---
diff --git a/dlls/advpack/advpack.c b/dlls/advpack/advpack.c
index 926d5e7..c80be4e 100644
--- a/dlls/advpack/advpack.c
+++ b/dlls/advpack/advpack.c
@@ -252,6 +252,8 @@ BOOL WINAPI IsNTAdmin(DWORD reserved, LPDWORD pReserved)
 
     for (i = 0; i < pTokenGroups->GroupCount; i++)
     {
+        /* Stained Glass OS 7737: enabled, not a filtered administrator's deny-only group */
+        if (!(pTokenGroups->Groups[i].Attributes & SE_GROUP_ENABLED)) continue;
         if (EqualSid(pSid, pTokenGroups->Groups[i].Sid))
         {
             bSidFound = TRUE;
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shellord.c b/dlls/shell32/shellord.c
index 3a0b952..1c9dcd8 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellord.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellord.c
@@ -1578,6 +1578,11 @@ BOOL WINAPI IsUserAnAdmin(VOID)
 
     for (i = 0; i < lpGroups->GroupCount; i++)
     {
+        /* Stained Glass OS 7737: an enabled Administrators group: a filtered administrator's token
+         * holds it only for deny, and Windows answers FALSE for it */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_ADMIN_BY_PRESENCE
+        if (!(lpGroups->Groups[i].Attributes & SE_GROUP_ENABLED)) continue;
+#endif
         if (EqualSid(lpSid, lpGroups->Groups[i].Sid))
         {
             bResult = TRUE;
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index b411329..20369a5 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -597,6 +597,23 @@ static int uid_in_group( uid_t uid, gid_t gid )
     return ret;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS 7737: is this account one of the machine's administrators? They are the members of
+ * the sg-admins group (Settings > Accounts; what the elevation broker asks consent of). On Windows such an
+ * account's ordinary token is split: Administrators only for deny, elevation type Limited, and a linked
+ * full token that consent hands out. */
+int sg_uid_is_admin( uid_t uid )
+{
+    struct group *gr;
+
+    /* the server's own environment, its owner's choice: a site (or a gate) that names its
+     * administrators' group differently */
+    const char *name = getenv( "SG_ADMIN_GROUP" );
+
+    if (!uid) return 0;
+    if (!(gr = getgrnam( name && *name ? name : "sg-admins" ))) return 0;
+    return uid_in_group( uid, gr->gr_gid );
+}
+
 /* Decide whether a connecting process may use this server.
  *
  * On an ordinary prefix this is not reached as a decision: the 0700 directory
